.TH LIBFAAR 3 "October 2026" "libfaar 3.0.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
libfaar, faar_create, faar_set_dither, faar_set_boundary, faar_get_delay, faar_process, faar_flush, faar_destroy \- CPU audio resampler library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <faar.h>
.sp
.BI "faar_handle_t faar_create(uint32_t " in_rate ", uint32_t " out_rate ", uint16_t " channels ", faar_quality_t " quality ");"
.sp
.BI "int faar_set_dither(faar_handle_t " handle ", faar_dither_t " dither ", uint8_t " target_bits ");"
.sp
.BI "int faar_set_boundary(faar_handle_t " handle ", faar_boundary_t " boundary ");"
.sp
.BI "size_t faar_get_delay(faar_handle_t " handle ");"
.sp
.BI "size_t faar_process(faar_handle_t " handle ", const float *" in_samples ", size_t " in_count ", float *" out_samples ", size_t " max_out_count ");"
.sp
.BI "size_t faar_flush(faar_handle_t " handle ", float *" out_samples ", size_t " max_out_count ");"
.sp
.BI "void faar_destroy(faar_handle_t " handle ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libfaar
is a C library for digital audio sample rate conversion. The staged-short CPU backend uses an overlap-save DFT prefilter and a rate-planned fractional-delay stage. Input and output are float PCM; staged-short uses double-precision filter and FFT arithmetic. Rejection and transition bandwidth depend on the quality preset and conversion ratio.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BR faar_create ()
Allocates and initializes a resampler instance for converting audio from \fIin_rate\fR to \fIout_rate\fR across \fIchannels\fR (1 to 8 channels supported). Quality presets include \fBFAAR_QUALITY_FAST\fR, \fBFAAR_QUALITY_GOOD\fR, and \fBFAAR_QUALITY_HIGH\fR. Float builds (\fB-Dfaar-precision=float\fR) support Fast and Good only; creation returns NULL for \fBFAAR_QUALITY_HIGH\fR.
.TP
.BR faar_set_dither ()
Configures dithering and noise-shaping error feedback (\fBFAAR_DITHER_OFF\fR, \fBFAAR_DITHER_TPDF\fR, or \fBFAAR_DITHER_SHAPED\fR) for quantization down to 16-bit or 24-bit integer PCM targets.
.TP
.BR faar_get_delay ()
Returns filter lookahead in input frames, including cascaded stages; zero at equal rates.
.TP
.BR faar_process ()
Resamples interleaved floating-point PCM audio samples. All supplied input is buffered. Drain pending output with a NULL input pointer and zero input count. Output time zero corresponds to input time zero. The selected boundary mode controls endpoint extension.
.TP
.BR faar_set_boundary ()
Selects how samples outside a finite input stream are extended. The default, \fBFAAR_BOUNDARY_HOLD\fR, continues the first and last sample; \fBFAAR_BOUNDARY_ZERO\fR uses silence. Set this before processing or flushing. Holding endpoints avoids forcing a step to silence at a nonzero endpoint, but cannot supply neighboring audio or keep a sample clock continuous across independent handles. Use one handle for a continuous stream.
.TP
.BR faar_flush ()
Flushes remaining pipeline history at end of stream. Call until zero is returned. Total output length is ceil(input_frames * out_rate / in_rate). No further input may be supplied after flushing starts.
.TP
.BR faar_destroy ()
Frees all allocated memory and resources associated with the resampler handle.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR faar (1),
.BR faac (1)
